# ZAVORA client environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Vite inlines VITE_* variables at BUILD time,
# so the dev server must be restarted after changing any of them.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored; never commit real credentials here. Server-side
# secrets (database password, CJ token) belong in server/config.js, not here —
# anything in a VITE_* variable is readable by the browser.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mock vs real API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# true  -> every service resolves from client/src/services/mockCatalogue.js.
#          No database or API server needed. This is the default.
# false -> every service calls the REST API. Requires:
#            1. MariaDB/MySQL running with the zavora schema applied
#            2. The API server started (cd server && npm start)
#            3. `npm run db:seed` to populate the catalogue
#
# PowerShell:  $env:VITE_USE_MOCK = 'false'; npm run dev
# bash:        VITE_USE_MOCK=false npm run dev
VITE_USE_MOCK=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API base URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "/api" works in development because the API enables CORS for
# http://localhost:5173 with credentials, and sends the session cookie.
# Point it at an absolute URL when the API is on another host.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api